WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.863
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.163 --> 00:00:08.804
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:15.820
Unit seventeen: Study Habits. Today you will talk about how you study using gerunds after prepositions.

4
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.494
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:22.666
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.517 --> 00:00:24.704
Study habit.

7
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:28.250
Study habit means a way you usually study.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.931
Making notes is a good study habit.

9
00:00:31.517 --> 00:00:34.239
Your turn. Say: Study habit.

10
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.240
Study habit.

11
00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:39.833
Focus.

12
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.604
Focus means to give all your attention to something.

13
00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:46.112
I focus better in a quiet room.

14
00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:49.148
Your turn. Say: Focus.

15
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.013
Focus.

16
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:54.832
Organize.

17
00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:58.385
Organize means to put things in a good order.

18
00:00:58.983 --> 00:01:01.134
I organize my books every Sunday.

19
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.368
Your turn. Say: Organize.

20
00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.292
Organize.

21
00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:09.923
Review.

22
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:13.160
Review means to study something again.

23
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.017
I review my notes before a test.

24
00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:18.770
Your turn. Say: Review.

25
00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:22.576
Review.

26
00:01:23.317 --> 00:01:24.341
Distraction.

27
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.232
Distraction means something that takes your attention away.

28
00:01:28.817 --> 00:01:31.037
My phone is my biggest distraction.

29
00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:34.326
Your turn. Say: Distraction.

30
00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.191
Distraction.

31
00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.218
Concentration.

32
00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:44.273
Concentration means the ability to think about one thing.

33
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:46.836
Noise breaks my concentration.

34
00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.369
Your turn. Say: Concentration.

35
00:01:53.233 --> 00:01:54.443
Concentration.

36
00:01:55.183 --> 00:01:56.173
Schedule.

37
00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.752
Schedule means a plan of times for activities.

38
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.779
I made a study schedule for the exams.

39
00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:05.966
Your turn. Say: Schedule.

40
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.824
Schedule.

41
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:11.596
Improve.

42
00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:14.502
Improve means to get better.

43
00:02:15.117 --> 00:02:17.557
My grades improve when I study every day.

44
00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:21.151
Your turn. Say: Improve.

45
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:24.978
Improve.

46
00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:29.626
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:33.110
Visal, what helps you focus when you study?

48
00:02:34.217 --> 00:02:37.726
I improve by reviewing my notes every night.

49
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:40.538
What about distractions?

50
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.498
I'm good at avoiding them. I put my phone in another room.

51
00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:47.933
Do you have a schedule?

52
00:02:49.017 --> 00:02:54.806
Yes. I'm interested in organizing my time well. It helps my concentration.

53
00:02:55.967 --> 00:02:57.839
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:58.683 --> 00:03:01.693
Grammar focus: Gerund after preposition.

55
00:03:01.993 --> 00:03:03.238
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.611
I improve my grades by reviewing every night.

57
00:03:07.517 --> 00:03:09.539
She is good at organizing her time.

58
00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.740
Before studying, I turn off my phone.

59
00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.197
After a preposition, always use the -ing form of a verb.

60
00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:22.599
Be careful! Don't say: I improve my grades by review every night.

61
00:03:24.533 --> 00:03:27.926
Say: I improve my grades by reviewing every night.

62
00:03:28.226 --> 00:03:30.678
After a preposition, use the -ing form.

63
00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.956
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:36.313
Good Study Habits.

65
00:03:36.613 --> 00:03:39.379
Good study habits start with organizing your time.

66
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:43.365
I make a schedule by writing my lessons on a calendar.

67
00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:48.804
Staying focused and avoiding distraction helps improve concentration.

68
00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.426
Before starting homework, I put my phone away.

69
00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:56.304
Reviewing your notes regularly makes a big difference.

70
00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:01.460
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.317 --> 00:04:04.467
I improve by blank every night.

72
00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:08.873
A, reviewing. B, review. C, to review.

73
00:04:12.433 --> 00:04:14.549
The answer is A: reviewing.

74
00:04:15.683 --> 00:04:18.333
Something that takes your attention away is a blank.

75
00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:22.565
A, distraction. B, schedule. C, focus.

76
00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.181
The answer is A: distraction.

77
00:04:29.317 --> 00:04:31.595
To study something again is to blank.

78
00:04:31.895 --> 00:04:35.989
A, review. B, organize. C, concentrate.

79
00:04:39.533 --> 00:04:41.626
The answer is A: review.

80
00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:45.938
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:46.783 --> 00:04:49.352
What is one study habit that helps you focus?

82
00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.581
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:59.881 --> 00:05:08.268
I focus better by studying in short sessions. I study for twenty-five minutes, then I take a five-minute break.

84
00:05:08.568 --> 00:05:10.370
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:11.283 --> 00:05:15.677
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and gerund after preposition.

86
00:05:15.977 --> 00:05:20.487
Today's value is discipline. Follow your routine, even when it is hard.

87
00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:23.405
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

88
00:05:23.705 --> 00:05:26.206
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

